## Why This Is Asked
Examines practical isolation controls for logs in multi-tenant cloud-native systems, including data-minimization, policy enforcement, and incident response.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped logging
- ABAC/OPA policy enforcement at ingestion
- Data redaction and least-privilege exporters
- SPIRE/mTLS between log agents and collectors
- Ephemeral credentials rotation and secrets hygiene

## Code Example
```javascript
function redactForTenant(log, tenantId) {
  const redacted = {...log};
  const sensitiveKeys = ['ssn','creditCard','dob','email'];
  for (const k of sensitiveKeys) {
    if (redacted[k] && redacted.tenantId === tenantId) {
      redacted[k] = '[REDACTED]';
    }
  }
  return redacted;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test for cross-tenant access in search results?
- What monitoring signals indicate redaction failures or policy drift?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design zero-trust controls across cloud and on‑prem, plus IR rigor.

## Key Concepts

- Least privilege across IAM and Kubernetes RBAC
- OIDC-based short-lived credentials and STS
- Image provenance and SBOM
- Secret management and CI rotation
- IR containment and customer notification

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: verify an OIDC-provided token expiration
function isTokenValid(token) {
  const now = Math.floor(Date.now()/1000);
  const payload = decodeJWT(token);
  return payload.exp > now;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the rotation workflow without impacting production?
- What metrics indicate readiness of the new controls?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design tenant-isolated logging, encryption, immutability, and incident response.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant log isolation and encryption
- Immutable/auditable logs with hash chaining
- Tenant-scoped alert routing
- CI gate validating logs against a schema
- 72-hour IR playbook for log leakage

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple envelope log example
function envelopeLog(event, prevHash, key) {
  const payload = JSON.stringify(event);
  const hash = sha256(prevHash + payload);
  const orc = encrypt(payload, key);
  return { payloadEnc: orc, hash, prevHash: hash };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test log isolation end-to-end?
- What are the performance implications of immutable logs and hashing?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests handling of edge ID management, data encryption, and strict multitenant data boundaries across cloud services. It requires concrete controls rather than abstractions.

## Key Concepts
- Edge IAM with audience-bound JWTs and gateway introspection
- Envelope encryption and per-tenant key rotation (KMS)
- Snowflake RBAC + Row-Level Security and per-tenant warehouses
- CI/CD secret scanning and misconfiguration checks
- IR playbooks with traceability and forensics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Verify JWT audience at edge
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');
function verify(token, expectedAud) {
  try {
    const decoded = jwt.verify(token, KEY, { audience: expectedAud });
    return decoded;
  } catch (e) {
    throw new Error('Unauthorized');
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you detect token reuse across tenants?
- What metrics indicate successful policy enforcement?

## Why This Is Asked

To assess practical control-plane hardening choices under real-world friction, focusing on mobile app token misuse and multi-tenant isolation.

## Key Concepts

- OAuth2/OIDC security best practices (PKCE, short TTLs)
- Token binding and device fingerprinting
- Token rotation and per-tenant scopes
- Token introspection and revocation
- Observability and IR readiness

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: rotate refresh token on use and bind to device and tenant
function onRefresh(token, deviceId, tenant) {
  if (!isValidDevice(token.bindInfo, deviceId, tenant)) throw new Error('invalid');
  const newToken = issueAccessToken(tenant, token.tenant);
  rotateRefreshToken(token.id);
  return { accessToken: newToken, refreshToken: getRotatedRefresh(token.id) };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the token binding mechanism in CI/CD?
- What metrics indicate token abuse and how would you respond?

## Why This Is Asked
The question probes practical edge device security, supply chain controls, and IR readiness for OTA updates in a fleet setting.

## Key Concepts
- Hardware root of trust and device attestation
- Per-release key rotation and role separation
- SBOMs and artifact signing for OTA safety
- OTA gateway revocation and device rollback
- Incident response, containment, and forensics timelines

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation: verify OTA signature before flash
function verifyAndApply(image, publicKey) {
  const ok = verifySignature(image, publicKey);
  if (!ok) throw new Error('Invalid OTA signature');
  flash(image);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale key rotation across millions of devices?
- What logging and forensics data would you collect for IR?
